The tam_v2 model is a fine-tuned version of Tesseract's Tamil model "tam" from
https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_best, licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

Training text and ground truth
- Proofread page text from Tamil Wikisource (https://ta.wikisource.org), by the Tamil
  Wikisource contributors, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The release files
  tam_v2-training-text.txt.gz, tam_v2-wordlist.txt.gz and tam_v2-real-lines.jsonl.gz contain
  this text and are shared under the same licence. Page links are in examples/wikisource-pages.json,
  books/books.json and the line list.
- tam.training_text from https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/langdata_lstm (Apache License 2.0),
  part of tam_v2-training-text.txt.gz.

Scanned page images
- Training lines were cut from page images held by the Internet Archive (https://archive.org),
  mostly copies of the Tamil Virtual Academy / Tamil Digital Library and the Digital Library of
  India. Test pages are Tamil Wikisource scans hosted by Wikimedia Commons. The images are not
  redistributed here; the line list says where each one can be downloaded.

Fonts
- tam_v2: text lines were rendered with 233 font styles. Their sources and licences are listed
  in examples/fonts-v2-open.md and models/tam_v2/fonts.json.
- tam_multifont (V1, research model, also fine-tuned from "tam"): 188 font styles, listed in
  models/tam_multifont/fonts.json. They include Latha (Microsoft, proprietary) and uniAmma-10,
  -11 and -16 (origin unknown), which have no open licence.
- tam_v2_research (V2-research, research model, also fine-tuned from "tam"): 276 font styles,
  listed in models/tam_v2_research/fonts.json. Besides Latha and uniAmma, they include 45 styles
  of the C-DAC GIST fonts ("Copyright (c) 2005, C-DAC, GIST PUNE, INDIA. FOR NON-COMMERCIAL FREE
  USAGE. For commercial license contact C-DAC, GIST, Pune."). The tam_v2_research model files
  are therefore licensed CC BY-NC 4.0, for non-commercial use only
  (models/tam_v2_research/LICENSE.md), not Apache-2.0.
- The fonts themselves are not redistributed.

Benchmarks
- RANLP 2025 synthetic Tamil OCR (https://huggingface.co/datasets/Nevidu/tamil_synthetic_ocr)
  and the Tamil OCR Benchmark (https://huggingface.co/datasets/mvbalaji/tamil-ocr-benchmark)
  were used for testing only. Only their scores, and line-group labels computed here, are
  included.
